# 14. GITHUB PAGES COMPATIBILITY

The completed project must be deployable to GitHub Pages as a static website.

Technical requirements:

- Use static HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, or a frontend framework that builds into static files.
- Do not require a backend server or database.
- Do not require an API key.
- Do not require an external AI service at runtime.
- Perform question generation and answer checking locally in the browser.
- Include all required configuration files and dependencies.
- Ensure all asset paths work under a repository subpath, such as `https://username.github.io/repository-name/`.
- Configure the base path correctly if using React, Vite, or another framework.
- Ensure refreshing the page does not cause routing errors.
- Use browser-compatible JavaScript.
- Avoid dependencies on services that require paid hosting.

If a math-rendering library is used, ensure it is loaded reliably and does not prevent the rest of the reviewer from functioning.

